
# E-Commerce Data Warehouse & Analytics

> 🚧 **Status: Work in Progress**

An e-commerce analytics and data-modeling project being developed entirely in **Kaggle Notebooks**, using Python, SQL, DuckDB, and Parquet.

The goal is to transform large-scale e-commerce behavioral data into a validated analytical data model, business insights, and reporting-ready datasets.

---

## Dataset

**Source:** [eCommerce Behavior Data from Multi-Category Store — Kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mkechinov/ecommerce-behavior-data-from-multi-category-store)

The dataset contains event-level online shopping behavior, including product views, cart activity, and purchases.

### Dataset Columns

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `event_time` | Timestamp of the event |
| `event_type` | Event type: `view`, `cart`, `remove_from_cart`, or `purchase` |
| `product_id` | Product identifier |
| `category_id` | Category identifier |
| `category_code` | Product category code |
| `brand` | Brand name |
| `price` | Recorded product price |
| `user_id` | User identifier |
| `user_session` | Session identifier |

**Processing note:** The complete dataset is very large. DuckDB will be used to process the data efficiently rather than loading the entire dataset into Pandas at once.

The exact files and schemas will be verified in the Kaggle environment before processing.

---

## Project Objectives

- Inspect and profile the source data.
- Validate data types, missing values, duplicates, timestamps, identifiers, and prices.
- Build a reproducible processing workflow inside Kaggle.
- Use DuckDB and Parquet for efficient analytical processing.
- Define data grain and design a dimensional model.
- Build and validate fact and dimension tables.
- Perform analytical SQL queries.
- Analyze customer, product, category, brand, session, and time-based behavior.
- Conduct funnel, RFM, cohort, and retention analysis.
- Generate documented business KPIs.
- Prepare analytical datasets for Power BI.

---

