## Important Analytical Assumptions

### Order Identification

The dataset does not provide a conventional explicit order ID. A session identifier must not automatically be treated as a true order ID without validating the source semantics.

If a session is used as an order proxy, that assumption and its limitations will be documented.

### Revenue Calculation

A purchase event's `price` is not necessarily equivalent to order-line revenue or total order value.

Revenue metrics will be explicitly defined, and double counting will be checked. Where the available fields do not support a definitive business measure, the result will be labeled as a proxy.

### Funnel Interpretation

Counts of events, distinct users, and distinct sessions represent different measures. Each funnel metric will state which unit it uses.

### Customer Identity

User-level analysis will account for missing identifiers and the limitations of interpreting observed user IDs as complete real-world customer identities.

